+- [x] 1.2 Add `OrderRepository.updateDiscount(id, { discountCents, finalAmountCents, couponCode })` and verify a test writes the row then reads it back with the new values
+- [x] 1.3 Add `CouponRepository.recordRedemption(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, createdAt)` and `incrementUsedCount(code)` and verify a test records a redemption and observes the incremented `usedCount`
+
+## 2. Redemption service and route wiring
+
+- [x] 2.1 Add `RedemptionService` that loads the order, validates the coupon, computes the discount, and persists order + redemption atomically; verify with an integration test asserting HTTP 200 and updated `discountCents` / `finalAmountCents` / `couponCode` on a valid `PERCENT` coupon
+- [x] 2.2 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` and wire `RedemptionService` in `createApp`; verify the route responds 200 to a valid request through `app.request(...)`
+- [x] 2.3 Verify a `FIXED` coupon applied end-to-end yields the expected `discountCents` and `finalAmountCents` in the response body
+
+## 3. Validation and rejection paths
+
+- [x] 3.1 Validate `couponCode` presence/type and order existence; verify missing/invalid `couponCode` returns 400 `INVALID_REQUEST` and an unknown order id returns 404 `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`
+- [x] 3.2 Reject unknown coupons (400 `COUPON_NOT_FOUND`), non-`ACTIVE` coupons (400 `COUPON_INACTIVE`), and coupons outside their validity window (400 `COUPON_EXPIRED` / `COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID`); verify each with a test using the injected fixed clock
+- [x] 3.3 Reject orders below `minAmountCents` with 400 `COUPON_MIN_AMOUNT_NOT_MET` and non-`PENDING` orders with 409 `ORDER_NOT_PENDING`; verify both with tests
+- [x] 3.4 Verify a successful application records exactly one redemption row linking the order and coupon
+
+## 4. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run `npm run build` (type check) and `npm test` and confirm the benchmark tests plus all new redemption tests pass
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change once implementation is reviewed and verified.
